156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 124 0 R
/T (        The key problem is that most targeted drug carriers can be misled. They release their medicine when they detect a single trigger, such as acidity or a particular enzyme, but inflamed or injured healthy tissue can produce the same signals. As a result, the drug may be released outside the tumor, exposing healthy cells to unnecessary harm. What is needed is a carrier that does not depend on just one signal. It should confirm that several tumorrelated signals are present together before releasing its drug, so that it can tell tumor tissue apart from normal tissue more reliably and deliver treatment only where it is needed. )
/E (        The key problem is that most targeted drug carriers can be misled. They release their medicine when they detect a single trigger, such as acidity or a particular enzyme, but inflamed or injured healthy tissue can produce the same signals. As a result, the drug may be released outside the tumor, exposing healthy cells to unnecessary harm. What is needed is a carrier that does not depend on just one signal. It should confirm that several tumorrelated signals are present together before releasing its drug, so that it can tell tumor tissue apart from normal tissue more reliably and deliver treatment only where it is needed. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
